#PROFILE UEFI
#TARGET X86_64
#RUNTIME NONE
#CALLCONV UEFI

' RFC-0045 Phase 4: substrate unification. A single fixture, running under APS's own CR3/GDT/IDT
' (reusing aps-gdt-reload.abas's own proven sequence) after a real ExitBootServices, genuinely
' running RFC-0007's own HELP/OT/?SYNTAX ERROR/backspace command loop -- fed by BOTH real input
' paths this RFC built: the Phase 1 PS/2 driver and the Phase 3 USB HID driver, polled together,
' whichever produces a real character first. Output moves from RFC-0007's own original ConsoleOut.
' Write (firmware-hosted, hangs after ExitBootServices per this RFC's own Section 4 finding) to the
' real serial port -- the only real, proven post-exit output channel anywhere in this project's own
' history (aps-gdt-reload.abas, ps2-keyboard-driver.abas). The READY. prompt itself is therefore a
' real serial terminal session under QEMU, not a graphical console -- a real, honestly-scoped
' substitution, not a silent one; a GOP-based text console is real future work, not attempted here.
'
' Both drivers' own setup (xHCI PCI discovery/MMIO/rings/enumeration needs BootServices.
' AllocatePages) happens BEFORE ExitBootServices, matching every other real constraint this project
' has already established for DMA-capable structures. PS2Keyboard.Init has no such dependency but
' is called at the same point for consistency. If no USB keyboard is attached, USB HID enumeration
' is allowed to fail closed (usbSlotId stays 0) and the combined poll loop simply never checks that
' path -- PS/2 alone is a real, correct configuration, not a failure (RFC-0045's own explicit
' "EITHER input path" requirement, proven by this fixture's own negative-control run).
'
' Frozen copies of stdlib/ps2_keyboard_policy.abas and stdlib/usb_xhci_policy.abas, plus the
' descriptor-table/ExitBootServices helpers from aps-gdt-reload.abas, are inlined below, matching
' this project's established no-include-system fixture convention.

' Real PS/2 Keyboard Driver (RFC-0045 Phase 1), raw port I/O only -- no UEFI protocol dependency,
' safe to call both before AND after ExitBootServices. Built to close a real, empirically-confirmed
' gap: RFC-0045 Section 4 found systemTable.ConsoleIn.ReadKeyStroke crashes (not merely hangs)
' after ExitBootServices, so the Polymorphic Substrate has no keyboard input path of its own
' without a driver that does not depend on any Boot-Services-backed protocol.


' --- Documented deviations, stated up front, same spirit as every other provider in this project. ---
'
' 1. Scan Code Set: this driver assumes Scan Code Set 1 (the i8042 controller's own standard
'    legacy-translation output, confirmed empirically against real QEMU/OVMF -- port 0x60 emitted
'    0x1E (make) then 0x9E (make+0x80, break) for a real injected 'a' keystroke, exactly Set 1's
'    own known encoding, not assumed from general PC hardware knowledge alone (RFC-0045 Section
'    7.1's own mandate). Real hardware could, in principle, differ -- this is exactly the kind of
'    finding a real hardware validation package (WP, RFC-0045 Phase 5) exists to surface.
'
' 2. Character coverage: US QWERTY, unshifted only (RFC-0045 Non-Goal 4/the same scope this
'    project's own existing QEMU keystroke-injection convention already uses). Shift/Ctrl/Alt
'    modifier tracking is real future work, not attempted here -- ScancodeToChar returns 0 (no
'    mapping) for modifier keys and anything this table does not define, matching this project's
'    own fail-closed-per-value precedent (e.g. UefiBlockDevice.Discover's own per-device fail
'    closed, not partial success).
'
' 3. Break codes (key release, make code + 0x80 in Set 1) are read and discarded, not translated --
'    PollScancode returns the raw byte including the break-code high bit so a caller COULD
'    distinguish make/break if it needed to, but ScancodeToChar only defines mappings for real make
'    codes (bit 7 clear); a caller that feeds a break code into ScancodeToChar gets 0 back, the same
'    "no mapping" result an actually-unmapped make code would produce -- deliberately unified,
'    since RFC-0007's own line-editing model only needs key-press events, not release events.

FUNCTION Ps2DataPort() AS IOPORT
    RETURN PORT.Address(96)    ' 0x60
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Ps2StatusPort() AS IOPORT
    RETURN PORT.Address(100)   ' 0x64
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Ps2CommandPort() AS IOPORT
    RETURN PORT.Address(100)   ' 0x64 (same port; a write here is a controller command, not data)
END FUNCTION

' Real, minimal, standard i8042 init: disable the second PS/2 port (in case a mouse is present --
' this driver only wants the keyboard's own byte stream, undisturbed by an interleaved mouse one),
' flush any stale pending byte, then explicitly (re-)enable the first PS/2 port. Does not depend on
' any UEFI protocol -- safe before or after ExitBootServices.
FUNCTION PS2Keyboard.Init() AS BOOL
    LET cmd AS IOPORT = Ps2CommandPort()
    LET status AS IOPORT = Ps2StatusPort()
    LET data AS IOPORT = Ps2DataPort()

    PORT.WriteByte(cmd, 167)   ' 0xA7, disable second PS/2 port

    LET flushAttempts AS U64 = 0
    WHILE flushAttempts < 1000
        LET flushStatus AS U8 = PORT.ReadByte(status)
        IF (flushStatus AND 1) <> 0 THEN
            PORT.ReadByte(data)
        END IF
        flushAttempts = flushAttempts + 1
    WEND

    PORT.WriteByte(cmd, 174)   ' 0xAE, enable first PS/2 port
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Returns 0 if no scancode byte is currently pending, otherwise the real raw byte read from the
' data port (including the Set 1 break-code high bit, 0x80, if this is a key-release byte) --
' callers that only care about key presses should check ScancodeToChar's own 0-for-no-mapping
' result rather than inspecting the high bit themselves, matching this driver's own established
' "make and break unify to the same no-op result for anything not a real make code" contract.
FUNCTION PS2Keyboard.PollScancode() AS U32
    LET status AS IOPORT = Ps2StatusPort()
    LET data AS IOPORT = Ps2DataPort()
    LET statusValue AS U8 = PORT.ReadByte(status)
    IF (statusValue AND 1) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET scancode AS U8 = PORT.ReadByte(data)
    LET scancodeAsU32 AS U32 = scancode
    RETURN scancodeAsU32
END FUNCTION

' Scan Code Set 1 make-code -> ASCII translation, US QWERTY, unshifted. Returns 0 for anything with
' no defined mapping (modifier keys, function keys, break codes, extended-sequence prefix byte
' 0xE0, etc.) -- a real, deliberate fail-closed result, not a guess.
FUNCTION PS2Keyboard.ScancodeToChar(scancode AS U32) AS U16
    IF scancode >= 128 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    IF scancode = 28 THEN
        RETURN 13
    END IF
    IF scancode = 14 THEN
        RETURN 8
    END IF
    IF scancode = 57 THEN
        RETURN 32
    END IF

    IF scancode = 2 THEN
        RETURN 49
    END IF
    IF scancode = 3 THEN
        RETURN 50
    END IF
    IF scancode = 4 THEN
        RETURN 51
    END IF
    IF scancode = 5 THEN
        RETURN 52
    END IF
    IF scancode = 6 THEN
        RETURN 53
    END IF
    IF scancode = 7 THEN
        RETURN 54
    END IF
    IF scancode = 8 THEN
        RETURN 55
    END IF
    IF scancode = 9 THEN
        RETURN 56
    END IF
    IF scancode = 10 THEN
        RETURN 57
    END IF
    IF scancode = 11 THEN
        RETURN 48
    END IF
    IF scancode = 12 THEN
        RETURN 45
    END IF
    IF scancode = 13 THEN
        RETURN 61
    END IF

    IF scancode = 16 THEN
        RETURN 113
    END IF
    IF scancode = 17 THEN
        RETURN 119
    END IF
    IF scancode = 18 THEN
        RETURN 101
    END IF
    IF scancode = 19 THEN
        RETURN 114
    END IF
    IF scancode = 20 THEN
        RETURN 116
    END IF
    IF scancode = 21 THEN
        RETURN 121
    END IF
    IF scancode = 22 THEN
        RETURN 117
    END IF
    IF scancode = 23 THEN
        RETURN 105
    END IF
    IF scancode = 24 THEN
        RETURN 111
    END IF
    IF scancode = 25 THEN
        RETURN 112
    END IF
    IF scancode = 26 THEN
        RETURN 91
    END IF
    IF scancode = 27 THEN
        RETURN 93
    END IF
    IF scancode = 43 THEN
        RETURN 92
    END IF

    IF scancode = 30 THEN
        RETURN 97
    END IF
    IF scancode = 31 THEN
        RETURN 115
    END IF
    IF scancode = 32 THEN
        RETURN 100
    END IF
    IF scancode = 33 THEN
        RETURN 102
    END IF
    IF scancode = 34 THEN
        RETURN 103
    END IF
    IF scancode = 35 THEN
        RETURN 104
    END IF
    IF scancode = 36 THEN
        RETURN 106
    END IF
    IF scancode = 37 THEN
        RETURN 107
    END IF
    IF scancode = 38 THEN
        RETURN 108
    END IF
    IF scancode = 39 THEN
        RETURN 59
    END IF
    IF scancode = 40 THEN
        RETURN 39
    END IF
    IF scancode = 41 THEN
        RETURN 96
    END IF

    IF scancode = 44 THEN
        RETURN 122
    END IF
    IF scancode = 45 THEN
        RETURN 120
    END IF
    IF scancode = 46 THEN
        RETURN 99
    END IF
    IF scancode = 47 THEN
        RETURN 118
    END IF
    IF scancode = 48 THEN
        RETURN 98
    END IF
    IF scancode = 49 THEN
        RETURN 110
    END IF
    IF scancode = 50 THEN
        RETURN 109
    END IF
    IF scancode = 51 THEN
        RETURN 44
    END IF
    IF scancode = 52 THEN
        RETURN 46
    END IF
    IF scancode = 53 THEN
        RETURN 47
    END IF

    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION


' Real xHCI (USB 3 Host Controller) driver (RFC-0045 Phase 2), raw PCI config space + MMIO only --
' no UEFI protocol dependency for the controller-programming path itself (PCI discovery uses real
' port I/O at 0xCF8/0xCFC, safe both before and after ExitBootServices; ring/DCBAA memory is
' allocated via BootServices.AllocatePages while Boot Services are still available, matching
' aps-gdt-reload.abas's own established precedent for APS-owned physical memory).


' --- Documented deviations and a real, confirmed compiler finding, stated up front. ---
'
' 1. A REAL COMPILER BUG found and worked around during this driver's own development: MEMORY.
'    Read16(ADDRESS.Offset(ptr, N)) returns 0 instead of the real value when `ptr` holds a HIGH
'    64-bit address (confirmed at a real xHCI MMIO base, 0xC000000000) -- MEMORY.Read32 and
'    MEMORY.Read8 through the exact same ADDRESS.Offset pattern at the exact same high address are
'    unaffected, and MEMORY.Read16 at a LOW address (a plain fixed scratch buffer) is ALSO
'    unaffected. Root cause traced into src/compiler/fission.cpp's normalize()/width_bits() and
'    load_value() -- not conclusively pinned down to one exact instruction, and NOT fixed here
'    (real, but not on RFC-0045's own critical path; the workaround below is reliable and simpler
'    than continuing that investigation). This driver therefore reads every 16-bit-or-narrower
'    hardware field via a real 32-bit-aligned MEMORY.Read32 plus SHR/AND, never MEMORY.Read16, on
'    any MMIO register. Worth a dedicated compiler-bug follow-up outside this RFC's own scope.
'
' 2. No general allocator exists on this backend -- every DMA-visible xHCI structure (Command Ring,
'    Event Ring, Event Ring Segment Table, Device Context Base Address Array) is allocated via a
'    real systemTable.BootServices.AllocatePages call (matching aps-gdt-reload.abas's own
'    established precedent for APS-owned physical memory), one full 4096-byte page each -- trivially
'    satisfying every xHCI alignment requirement (64-byte minimum for rings/DCBAA), simple over
'    minimal.
'
' 3. Scoped to exactly what RFC-0045 Phase 2 requires: PCI discovery, MMIO mapping, controller
'    reset, minimal ring/DCBAA setup, starting the controller, and port enumeration/reset. Device
'    slot enable/address/configure (the rest of real USB device enumeration) is RFC-0045 Phase 3's
'    own scope, not this file's.

FUNCTION XhciStateAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(41943040))   ' 0x2800000, this driver's own scratch state
END FUNCTION

' State layout: PCI Bus/Device/Function (U32 each, +0/+4/+8), MMIO base physical address (U64,
' +16), mapped MMIO pointer (U64, +24), CAPLENGTH (U32, +32), operational-register base (U64,
' +40), runtime-register base (U64, +48), doorbell-register base (U64, +56), MaxSlots (U32, +64),
' MaxPorts (U32, +68), Command Ring physical/virtual (U64 each, +72/+80), Event Ring physical/
' virtual (U64 each, +88/+96), ERST physical/virtual (U64 each, +104/+112), DCBAA physical/virtual
' (U64 each, +120/+128), Command Ring cycle-bit state (U32, +136), Command Ring enqueue index (U32,
' +140), Event Ring dequeue index (U32, +144), Event Ring consumer cycle-bit state (U32, +148).
FUNCTION XhciPciBusAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN XhciStateAddress()
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciPciDeviceAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 4)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciPciFunctionAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 8)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciMmioBasePhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 16)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciMmioMappedAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 24)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciCapLengthAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 32)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciOpBaseAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 40)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciRuntimeBaseAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 48)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciDoorbellBaseAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 56)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciMaxSlotsAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 64)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciMaxPortsAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 68)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciCmdRingPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 72)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciCmdRingVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 80)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEventRingPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 88)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEventRingVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 96)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciErstPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 104)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciErstVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 112)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciDcbaaPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 120)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciDcbaaVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 128)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciCmdCycleStateAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 136)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciCmdEnqueueIndexAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 140)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEventDequeueIndexAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 144)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEventCycleStateAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 148)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciContextSizeAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 152)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION PciConfigAddressPort() AS IOPORT
    RETURN PORT.Address(3320)   ' 0xCF8
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION PciConfigDataPort() AS IOPORT
    RETURN PORT.Address(3324)   ' 0xCFC
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION PciConfigReadU32(bus AS U32, device AS U32, func AS U32, offset AS U32) AS U32
    LET address AS U32 = 2147483648
    address = address OR (bus SHL 16)
    address = address OR (device SHL 11)
    address = address OR (func SHL 8)
    address = address OR (offset AND 252)
    LET addrPort AS IOPORT = PciConfigAddressPort()
    LET dataPort AS IOPORT = PciConfigDataPort()
    PORT.WriteDWord(addrPort, address)
    LET value AS U32 = PORT.ReadDWord(dataPort)
    RETURN value
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION PciConfigWriteU32(bus AS U32, device AS U32, func AS U32, offset AS U32, value AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET address AS U32 = 2147483648
    address = address OR (bus SHL 16)
    address = address OR (device SHL 11)
    address = address OR (func SHL 8)
    address = address OR (offset AND 252)
    LET addrPort AS IOPORT = PciConfigAddressPort()
    LET dataPort AS IOPORT = PciConfigDataPort()
    PORT.WriteDWord(addrPort, address)
    PORT.WriteDWord(dataPort, value)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Real 32-bit-aligned MMIO field extraction -- see deviation #1 above. widthBits must be 8, 16, or
' 32; bitOffset is the field's own starting bit within the containing 32-bit word.
FUNCTION MmioReadField32(mapped AS MMIOPTR, byteOffset AS U32, bitOffset AS U32, widthBits AS U32) AS U32
    LET alignedOffset AS U32 = byteOffset AND 4294967292
    LET word AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(mapped, alignedOffset))
    LET extraShift AS U32 = (byteOffset AND 3) * 8
    LET totalShift AS U32 = extraShift + bitOffset
    LET shifted AS U32 = word SHR totalShift
    LET mask AS U32 = 4294967295
    IF widthBits < 32 THEN
        mask = (1 SHL widthBits) - 1
    END IF
    RETURN shifted AND mask
END FUNCTION

' Real PCI bus scan (RFC-0045 Section 6.1, point 1): Class=0x0C (Serial Bus Controller),
' Subclass=0x03 (USB), ProgIf=0x30 (XHCI). Stores Bus/Device/Function in state on success.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.DiscoverPci(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable) AS BOOL
    LET found AS BOOL = 0
    LET bus AS U32 = 0
    WHILE bus < 256
        IF found = 0 THEN
            LET device AS U32 = 0
            WHILE device < 32
                IF found = 0 THEN
                    LET func AS U32 = 0
                    WHILE func < 8
                        IF found = 0 THEN
                            LET vendorDevice AS U32 = PciConfigReadU32(bus, device, func, 0)
                            LET vendorId AS U32 = vendorDevice AND 65535
                            IF vendorId <> 65535 THEN
                                LET classReg AS U32 = PciConfigReadU32(bus, device, func, 8)
                                LET baseClass AS U32 = (classReg SHR 24) AND 255
                                LET subclass AS U32 = (classReg SHR 16) AND 255
                                LET progIf AS U32 = (classReg SHR 8) AND 255
                                IF baseClass = 12 THEN
                                    IF subclass = 3 THEN
                                        IF progIf = 48 THEN
                                            found = 1
                                            MEMORY.Write32(XhciPciBusAddress(), bus)
                                            MEMORY.Write32(XhciPciDeviceAddress(), device)
                                            MEMORY.Write32(XhciPciFunctionAddress(), func)
                                        END IF
                                    END IF
                                END IF
                            END IF
                        END IF
                        func = func + 1
                    WEND
                END IF
                device = device + 1
            WEND
        END IF
        bus = bus + 1
    WEND
    RETURN found
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION XhciDisconnectGuidAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 320)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciDisconnectHandlesAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 336)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciDisconnectIfaceAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 464)
END FUNCTION

' A REAL, confirmed root cause found via QEMU's own trace events (RFC-0045 Phase 3): OVMF's own
' native XHCI driver stays bound to this controller (it is a real PCI device firmware discovers
' and binds a driver to during its own boot-time driver-connection pass) and keeps periodically
' touching it -- QEMU's trace log showed spurious, unexplained repeated command-doorbell writes
' with no corresponding call anywhere in this driver, interleaved with this driver's own real
' commands, racing for the same Command Ring. This function finds the SAME PCI Bus/Device/Function
' this driver's own raw config-space scan (UsbXhci.DiscoverPci) already identified -- via
' EFI_PCI_IO_PROTOCOL's own GetLocation method, the only way to map a raw PCI location back to the
' EFI_HANDLE firmware knows it by -- and calls BootServices.DisconnectController on it, forcing
' UEFI's own driver stack off before this driver starts touching the controller's own registers.
' Real, honest fail-open: if no matching handle is found (already disconnected, or firmware never
' bound one), this returns FALSE without touching anything else -- not a hard requirement upstream.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.DisconnectFirmwareDriver(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable) AS BOOL
    LET guidBuf AS MMIOPTR = XhciDisconnectGuidAddress()
    MEMORY.Write64(guidBuf, 5522935658814222848)
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(guidBuf, 8), 11097520664359398558)

    LET maxHandles AS U64 = 16
    LET bufferSize AS U64 = maxHandles * 8
    LET bufferSizeAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(bufferSize)
    LET handleBuffer AS MMIOPTR = XhciDisconnectHandlesAddress()

    LET status AS U64 = systemTable.BootServices.LocateHandle(2, guidBuf, 0, bufferSizeAddr, handleBuffer)
    IF status <> 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    LET foundCount AS U64 = bufferSize \ 8
    IF foundCount > maxHandles THEN
        foundCount = maxHandles
    END IF

    LET targetBus AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciPciBusAddress())
    LET targetDevice AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciPciDeviceAddress())
    LET targetFunction AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciPciFunctionAddress())

    LET disconnected AS BOOL = 0
    LET i AS U64 = 0
    WHILE i < foundCount
        LET handleEntry AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(handleBuffer, i * 8)
        LET handle AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(handleEntry)
        LET ifaceOutAddr AS MMIOPTR = XhciDisconnectIfaceAddress()
        LET hpStatus AS U64 = systemTable.BootServices.HandleProtocol(handle, guidBuf, ifaceOutAddr)
        IF hpStatus = 0 THEN
            LET pciIo AS UEFI.PciIoProtocol = MEMORY.Read64(ifaceOutAddr)
            LET segOut AS U64 = 0
            LET segOutAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(segOut)
            LET busOut AS U64 = 0
            LET busOutAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(busOut)
            LET devOut AS U64 = 0
            LET devOutAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(devOut)
            LET funcOut AS U64 = 0
            LET funcOutAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(funcOut)
            LET glStatus AS U64 = pciIo.GetLocation(segOutAddr, busOutAddr, devOutAddr, funcOutAddr)
            IF glStatus = 0 THEN
                LET busU32 AS U32 = busOut
                LET devU32 AS U32 = devOut
                LET funcU32 AS U32 = funcOut
                IF busU32 = targetBus THEN
                    IF devU32 = targetDevice THEN
                        IF funcU32 = targetFunction THEN
                            systemTable.BootServices.DisconnectController(handle, 0, 0)
                            disconnected = 1
                        END IF
                    END IF
                END IF
            END IF
        END IF
        i = i + 1
    WEND
    RETURN disconnected
END FUNCTION

' Reads BAR0 (a real 64-bit MMIO BAR, per empirical confirmation against real QEMU qemu-xhci),
' enables Memory Space + Bus Master in the Command register, maps the MMIO region, and reads the
' Capability Registers this driver needs (CAPLENGTH, MaxSlots, MaxPorts). Real, confirmed fix
' (RFC-0045 Phase 3): disconnects firmware's own native XHCI driver from this controller FIRST,
' via UsbXhci.DisconnectFirmwareDriver -- see that function's own header comment for the full,
' QEMU-trace-confirmed finding this closes (a real firmware-vs-guest-driver ownership conflict).
FUNCTION UsbXhci.MapMmio(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable) AS BOOL
    UsbXhci.DisconnectFirmwareDriver(systemTable)

    LET bus AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciPciBusAddress())
    LET device AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciPciDeviceAddress())
    LET func AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciPciFunctionAddress())

    LET bar0 AS U32 = PciConfigReadU32(bus, device, func, 16)
    LET barType AS U32 = (bar0 SHR 1) AND 3
    LET mmioBaseLow AS U32 = bar0 AND 4294967280
    LET mmioBaseHigh AS U32 = 0
    IF barType = 2 THEN
        mmioBaseHigh = PciConfigReadU32(bus, device, func, 20)
    END IF

    LET commandReg AS U32 = PciConfigReadU32(bus, device, func, 4)
    PciConfigWriteU32(bus, device, func, 4, commandReg OR 6)

    LET mmioBaseHighAsU64 AS U64 = mmioBaseHigh
    LET mmioBaseLowAsU64 AS U64 = mmioBaseLow
    LET mmioBase AS U64 = (mmioBaseHighAsU64 SHL 32) OR mmioBaseLowAsU64
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciMmioBasePhysAddress(), mmioBase)

    LET mmioBasePhys AS PHYSICALPTR = mmioBase
    LET mapped AS MMIOPTR = MEMORY.MapDevice(mmioBasePhys, 65536)
    LET mappedAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(mapped)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciMmioMappedAddress(), mappedAsU64)

    LET capLength AS U32 = MmioReadField32(mapped, 0, 0, 8)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciCapLengthAddress(), capLength)

    LET hcsParams1 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(mapped, 4))
    LET maxSlots AS U32 = hcsParams1 AND 255
    LET maxPorts AS U32 = (hcsParams1 SHR 24) AND 255
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciMaxSlotsAddress(), maxSlots)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciMaxPortsAddress(), maxPorts)

    ' HCCPARAMS1.CSZ (bit 2): real Context Size (32 vs 64 bytes) -- verified from the real
    ' controller's own report, not assumed, matching this driver's own established discipline.
    LET hccParams1 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(mapped, 16))
    LET csz AS U32 = (hccParams1 SHR 2) AND 1
    LET contextSize AS U32 = 32
    IF csz = 1 THEN
        contextSize = 64
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciContextSizeAddress(), contextSize)

    LET capLengthAsU64 AS U64 = capLength
    LET opBase AS U64 = mappedAsU64 + capLengthAsU64
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciOpBaseAddress(), opBase)

    LET dboff AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(mapped, 20))
    LET dboffAligned AS U32 = dboff AND 4294967292
    LET dboffAsU64 AS U64 = dboffAligned
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciDoorbellBaseAddress(), mappedAsU64 + dboffAsU64)

    LET rtsoff AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(mapped, 24))
    LET rtsoffAligned AS U32 = rtsoff AND 4294967040
    LET rtsoffAsU64 AS U64 = rtsoffAligned
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciRuntimeBaseAddress(), mappedAsU64 + rtsoffAsU64)

    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Allocates one real page (BootServices.AllocatePages, type 0=AllocateAnyPages, memory type
' 2=EfiLoaderData, matching aps-gdt-reload.abas's own established call shape) and zeroes it.
' Returns the real physical address via outPhysAddress.
FUNCTION XhciAllocPage(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable, outPhysAddress AS PTR) AS BOOL
    LET pageStatus AS U64 = systemTable.BootServices.AllocatePages(0, 2, 1, outPhysAddress)
    RETURN pageStatus = 0
END FUNCTION

' Real controller reset (RFC-0045 Section 6.1, point 3): set HCRST, wait for it to self-clear,
' then wait for CNR (Controller Not Ready) to clear -- both real, required xHCI conditions before
' any register beyond USBCMD/USBSTS may be touched.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.Reset(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable) AS BOOL
    LET opBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciOpBaseAddress())
    LET opBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(opBase))

    MEMORY.Write32(opBaseMmio, 2)   ' USBCMD.HCRST

    ' Real early-exit polling idiom (this project's own established pattern for a busy-wait
    ' without a real BREAK/EXIT WHILE statement): jump the counter straight to the ceiling the
    ' instant the condition is met, rather than letting the loop keep iterating to the ceiling
    ' regardless -- a real, measured regression was found and fixed here: an earlier version
    ' checked the condition but never short-circuited, so even a SUCCESSFUL reset (which
    ' completes almost immediately in practice) still burned the full iteration ceiling every
    ' time; harmless at a small ceiling with a tight loop body, but genuinely blew a real QEMU
    ' harness's own timeout once the ceiling was raised and CPU.Pause was added per iteration.
    LET resetCeiling AS U64 = 2000000
    LET resetAttempts AS U64 = 0
    LET resetCleared AS BOOL = 0
    WHILE resetAttempts < resetCeiling
        LET cmd AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(opBaseMmio)
        IF (cmd AND 2) = 0 THEN
            resetCleared = 1
            resetAttempts = resetCeiling
        ELSE
            CPU.Pause
            resetAttempts = resetAttempts + 1
        END IF
    WEND
    IF resetCleared = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    LET cnrCeiling AS U64 = 2000000
    LET cnrAttempts AS U64 = 0
    LET cnrCleared AS BOOL = 0
    WHILE cnrAttempts < cnrCeiling
        LET status AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, 4))
        IF (status AND 2048) = 0 THEN
            cnrCleared = 1
            cnrAttempts = cnrCeiling
        ELSE
            CPU.Pause
            cnrAttempts = cnrAttempts + 1
        END IF
    WEND
    RETURN cnrCleared
END FUNCTION

' Real minimal ring/DCBAA setup (RFC-0045 Section 6.1, point 3): a one-page Command Ring
' (terminated with a real Link TRB pointing back to its own start, Toggle Cycle bit set), a
' one-page Event Ring plus a one-entry Event Ring Segment Table, and the Device Context Base
' Address Array -- CRCR/DCBAAP/ERSTSZ/ERSTBA/ERDP/CONFIG all programmed per spec.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.SetupRings(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable) AS BOOL
    LET cmdRingPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET cmdRingPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(cmdRingPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, cmdRingPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET cmdRingMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(cmdRingPhys))
    LET zeroIndex AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroIndex < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(cmdRingMmio, zeroIndex * 16), 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(cmdRingMmio, zeroIndex * 16 + 8), 0)
        zeroIndex = zeroIndex + 1
    WEND
    ' Real Link TRB at the ring's own last slot (index 255): Type=6 (Link), Toggle Cycle bit set,
    ' pointing back to the ring's own start -- the standard xHCI single-segment ring-wrap pattern.
    LET linkTrbOffset AS U32 = 255 * 16
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(cmdRingMmio, linkTrbOffset), cmdRingPhys)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(cmdRingMmio, linkTrbOffset + 8), 0)
    LET linkControl AS U32 = 1
    linkControl = linkControl OR (6 SHL 10)
    linkControl = linkControl OR 2
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(cmdRingMmio, linkTrbOffset + 12), linkControl)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciCmdRingPhysAddress(), cmdRingPhys)
    LET cmdRingMmioAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(cmdRingMmio)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciCmdRingVirtAddress(), cmdRingMmioAsU64)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciCmdCycleStateAddress(), 1)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciCmdEnqueueIndexAddress(), 0)

    LET eventRingPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET eventRingPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(eventRingPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, eventRingPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET eventRingMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(eventRingPhys))
    LET zeroIndex2 AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroIndex2 < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(eventRingMmio, zeroIndex2 * 16), 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(eventRingMmio, zeroIndex2 * 16 + 8), 0)
        zeroIndex2 = zeroIndex2 + 1
    WEND
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciEventRingPhysAddress(), eventRingPhys)
    LET eventRingMmioAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(eventRingMmio)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciEventRingVirtAddress(), eventRingMmioAsU64)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciEventDequeueIndexAddress(), 0)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciEventCycleStateAddress(), 1)

    LET erstPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET erstPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(erstPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, erstPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET erstMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(erstPhys))
    MEMORY.Write64(erstMmio, eventRingPhys)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(erstMmio, 8), 256)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(erstMmio, 12), 0)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciErstPhysAddress(), erstPhys)

    LET dcbaaPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET dcbaaPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(dcbaaPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, dcbaaPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET dcbaaMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(dcbaaPhys))
    LET zeroIndex3 AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroIndex3 < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(dcbaaMmio, zeroIndex3 * 8), 0)
        zeroIndex3 = zeroIndex3 + 1
    WEND
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciDcbaaPhysAddress(), dcbaaPhys)

    LET opBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciOpBaseAddress())
    LET opBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(opBase))

    LET maxSlots AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciMaxSlotsAddress())
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, 56), maxSlots)   ' CONFIG.MaxSlotsEn

    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, 48), dcbaaPhys)   ' DCBAAP

    LET crcrValue AS U64 = cmdRingPhys OR 1
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, 24), crcrValue)   ' CRCR, RCS=1

    LET runtimeBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciRuntimeBaseAddress())
    LET runtimeBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(runtimeBase))
    LET interrupter0 AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(runtimeBaseMmio, 32)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(interrupter0, 8), 1)          ' ERSTSZ = 1 segment
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(interrupter0, 16), erstPhys)  ' ERSTBA
    LET erdpValue AS U64 = eventRingPhys OR 8
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(interrupter0, 24), erdpValue) ' ERDP, EHB acknowledged

    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Real controller start (RFC-0045 Section 6.1, point 3): set USBCMD.RS, confirm USBSTS.HCH clears
' -- the real "controller is now running" proof, independent of any device/port work.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.Start() AS BOOL
    LET opBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciOpBaseAddress())
    LET opBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(opBase))

    LET cmd AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(opBaseMmio)
    MEMORY.Write32(opBaseMmio, cmd OR 1)   ' USBCMD.RS

    LET startCeiling AS U64 = 2000000
    LET attempts AS U64 = 0
    LET running AS BOOL = 0
    WHILE attempts < startCeiling
        LET status AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, 4))
        IF (status AND 1) = 0 THEN
            running = 1
            attempts = startCeiling
        ELSE
            CPU.Pause
            attempts = attempts + 1
        END IF
    WEND
    RETURN running
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION UsbXhci.MaxPorts() AS U32
    RETURN MEMORY.Read32(XhciMaxPortsAddress())
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION UsbXhci.ContextSize() AS U32
    RETURN MEMORY.Read32(XhciContextSizeAddress())
END FUNCTION

' Real port enumeration (RFC-0045 Section 6.1, point 4): PORTSC for port N (1-based) lives at
' operational-base + 0x400 + (N-1)*0x10. CCS (Current Connect Status) is bit 0.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.PortConnected(portIndex AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET opBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciOpBaseAddress())
    LET opBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(opBase))
    LET portOffset AS U32 = 1024 + (portIndex - 1) * 16
    LET portsc AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, portOffset))
    RETURN portsc AND 1
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION UsbXhci.PortRaw(portIndex AS U32) AS U32
    LET opBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciOpBaseAddress())
    LET opBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(opBase))
    LET portOffset AS U32 = 1024 + (portIndex - 1) * 16
    RETURN MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, portOffset))
END FUNCTION

' Real port reset (RFC-0045 Section 6.1, point 4): set PR (Port Reset, bit 4), wait for PRC (Port
' Reset Change, bit 21) to assert, then confirm PED (Port Enabled/Disabled, bit 1) is set.
'
' A real, intermittent bug found and fixed during this driver's own development: an earlier
' version preserved only bits 31:16 of the current PORTSC value (AND 0xFFFF0000) before writing
' PR -- which zeroed bit 9 (PP, Port Power, a real RW bit living in the LOWER 16 bits) as an
' unintended side effect, powering the port off on every reset attempt. QEMU's own xHCI emulation
' tolerated this most of the time (3/3 manual runs passed) but not always -- confirmed by a real
' failure surfacing only under a smoke test's own repeated-run harness, not manual testing. Fixed
' by preserving ONLY the specific bits that must survive a PR write (PLS bits 8:5, PP bit 9, PIC
' bits 15:14 -- mask 0xC3E0) and explicitly zeroing everything else, including every RW1C
' status-change bit (CSC/PEC/WRC/OCC/PRC/PLC/CEC) and the read-only CCS/PED/OCA bits, rather than
' blindly copying forward whatever the current register happened to contain.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.ResetPort(portIndex AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET opBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciOpBaseAddress())
    LET opBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(opBase))
    LET portOffset AS U32 = 1024 + (portIndex - 1) * 16
    LET portReg AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(opBaseMmio, portOffset)

    LET current AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(portReg)
    LET preserveMask AS U32 = 50144   ' 0xC3E0: PLS(8:5), PP(9), PIC(15:14)
    LET writeValue AS U32 = (current AND preserveMask) OR 16   ' OR in PR
    MEMORY.Write32(portReg, writeValue)

    LET prcCeiling AS U64 = 2000000
    LET attempts AS U64 = 0
    LET prcSeen AS BOOL = 0
    WHILE attempts < prcCeiling
        LET status AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(portReg)
        IF (status AND 2097152) <> 0 THEN
            prcSeen = 1
            attempts = prcCeiling
        ELSE
            CPU.Pause
            attempts = attempts + 1
        END IF
    WEND
    IF prcSeen = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    LET afterReset AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(portReg)
    RETURN (afterReset AND 2) <> 0
END FUNCTION

' ==========================================================================================
' RFC-0045 Phase 3: real USB device enumeration on top of the controller (Phase 2's own scope) --
' Enable Slot, Address Device, real control transfers (GET_DESCRIPTOR), Configure Endpoint, and
' real USB HID boot-protocol keyboard report polling. Extends the state region above with new
' fields starting at offset 160 (8-byte aligned): Input Context phys/virt (+160/+168), Device
' Context virt/phys (+176/+184), EP0 Transfer Ring phys/virt/cycle/enqueue (+192/+200/+208/+212),
' Interrupt Transfer Ring phys/virt/cycle/enqueue (+216/+224/+232/+236), Device Slot ID (+240),
' EP0 Max Packet Size (+244), Interrupt Endpoint Address/MaxPacketSize/Interval/ContextIndex
' (+248/+252/+256/+260), a 16-byte scratch event-TRB buffer (+264), and a 256-byte scratch DMA
' buffer for descriptor reads and HID reports (+280) -- all within the same identity-mapped
' scratch page every other field in this file already uses, safe as a real DMA target for the
' same reason every other structure in this file is (ordinary, physically-backed RAM).
' ==========================================================================================

FUNCTION XhciInputCtxPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 160)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciInputCtxVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 168)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciDeviceCtxVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 176)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciDeviceCtxPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 184)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEp0RingPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 192)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEp0RingVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 200)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEp0CycleStateAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 208)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEp0EnqueueIndexAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 212)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntRingPhysAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 216)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntRingVirtAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 224)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntCycleStateAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 232)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntEnqueueIndexAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 236)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciSlotIdAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 240)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciEp0MaxPacketAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 244)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntEndpointAddrAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 248)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntMaxPacketAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 252)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntIntervalAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 256)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciIntContextIndexAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 260)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciScratchEventBufferAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 264)
END FUNCTION
' The scratch DMA target buffer for descriptor reads and HID reports is NOT the fixed low scratch
' region directly (unlike every other field on this page) -- a device's own bus-mastering DMA needs
' a REAL physical address, and this driver's own established discipline (Command/Event rings, ERST,
' DCBAA, Input/Device Contexts, Transfer Rings) never assumes virt==phys for a fixed low address,
' always tracking a real BootServices.AllocatePages-returned physical address explicitly instead.
' These two fields cache that real allocation's own phys/virt pair once made (offsets 280/288);
' XhciEnsureScratchDmaBuffer lazily allocates it exactly once.
FUNCTION XhciScratchDmaPhysStorageAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 280)
END FUNCTION
FUNCTION XhciScratchDmaVirtStorageAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 288)
END FUNCTION

' Tracks whether a Normal TRB is already outstanding on the Interrupt IN endpoint's own Transfer
' Ring -- lets UsbHidKeyboard.PollReport stay non-blocking (PS2Keyboard.PollScancode's own sibling
' contract) without ever submitting a duplicate request while one is still in flight.
FUNCTION XhciIntRequestPendingAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.Offset(XhciStateAddress(), 312)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION XhciEnsureScratchDmaBuffer(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable) AS BOOL
    LET existingPhys AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciScratchDmaPhysStorageAddress())
    IF existingPhys <> 0 THEN
        RETURN 1
    END IF
    LET newPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET newPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(newPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, newPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciScratchDmaPhysStorageAddress(), newPhys)
    LET newMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(newPhys))
    LET newMmioAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(newMmio)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciScratchDmaVirtStorageAddress(), newMmioAsU64)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION XhciScratchDmaPhys() AS U64
    RETURN MEMORY.Read64(XhciScratchDmaPhysStorageAddress())
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION XhciScratchDmaMmio() AS MMIOPTR
    LET virt AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciScratchDmaVirtStorageAddress())
    RETURN ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(virt))
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION XhciRingDoorbell(slotOrHost AS U32, target AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET doorbellBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciDoorbellBaseAddress())
    LET doorbellBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(doorbellBase))
    LET doorbellReg AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(doorbellBaseMmio, slotOrHost * 4)
    MEMORY.Write32(doorbellReg, target)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Consumes and returns (via out16ByteBuffer) the NEXT event TRB if one is pending -- a real event
' is only "new" if its own Cycle bit matches this consumer's own currently-expected cycle state
' (the real xHCI event-ring consumption protocol). Advances the dequeue index/ERDP and toggles the
' expected cycle state on ring wrap. Returns FALSE (buffer untouched) if nothing new is pending.
FUNCTION XhciPollEvent(out16ByteBuffer AS MMIOPTR) AS BOOL
    LET eventRingVirt AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciEventRingVirtAddress())
    LET dequeueIndex AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciEventDequeueIndexAddress())
    LET expectedCycle AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciEventCycleStateAddress())
    LET eventRingMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(eventRingVirt))
    LET trbOffset AS U32 = dequeueIndex * 16
    LET trb AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(eventRingMmio, trbOffset)

    LET dword3 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 12))
    LET actualCycle AS U32 = dword3 AND 1
    IF actualCycle <> expectedCycle THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    MEMORY.Write64(out16ByteBuffer, MEMORY.Read64(trb))
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(out16ByteBuffer, 8), MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 8)))
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(out16ByteBuffer, 12), dword3)

    LET newIndex AS U32 = dequeueIndex + 1
    IF newIndex >= 256 THEN
        newIndex = 0
        LET newCycle AS U32 = 1 - expectedCycle
        MEMORY.Write32(XhciEventCycleStateAddress(), newCycle)
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciEventDequeueIndexAddress(), newIndex)

    LET runtimeBase AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciRuntimeBaseAddress())
    LET runtimeBaseMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(runtimeBase))
    LET interrupter0 AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(runtimeBaseMmio, 32)
    LET eventRingPhys AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciEventRingPhysAddress())
    LET newIndexAsU64 AS U64 = newIndex
    LET newDequeuePhys AS U64 = eventRingPhys + (newIndexAsU64 * 16)
    LET erdpValue AS U64 = newDequeuePhys OR 8
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(interrupter0, 24), erdpValue)

    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Enqueues one Command TRB (dword0/1/2 verbatim, controlBits combining TRB Type/Slot ID/other
' command-specific flags -- cycle bit added automatically) on the Command Ring, rings the Command
' doorbell, then polls for the matching Command Completion Event. Real ring-wrap handling: the
' Command Ring's own permanent Link TRB (slot 255, set up by SetupRings) has its Cycle bit
' toggled to match on wrap, exactly as real xHCI ring-management requires.
FUNCTION XhciSubmitCommand(dword0 AS U32, dword1 AS U32, dword2 AS U32, controlBits AS U32, outCompletionCode AS PTR, outSlotId AS PTR) AS BOOL
    LET cmdRingVirt AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciCmdRingVirtAddress())
    LET enqueueIndex AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciCmdEnqueueIndexAddress())
    LET cycleState AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciCmdCycleStateAddress())
    LET cmdRingMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(cmdRingVirt))
    LET trbOffset AS U32 = enqueueIndex * 16
    LET trb AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(cmdRingMmio, trbOffset)

    MEMORY.Write32(trb, dword0)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 4), dword1)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 8), dword2)
    LET dword3 AS U32 = controlBits OR cycleState
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 12), dword3)

    LET newIndex AS U32 = enqueueIndex + 1
    IF newIndex >= 255 THEN
        LET linkTrb AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(cmdRingMmio, 255 * 16)
        LET linkControl AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(linkTrb, 12))
        LET linkControlBase AS U32 = linkControl AND 4294967294
        LET newCycle AS U32 = 1 - cycleState
        MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(linkTrb, 12), linkControlBase OR newCycle)
        MEMORY.Write32(XhciCmdCycleStateAddress(), newCycle)
        newIndex = 0
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciCmdEnqueueIndexAddress(), newIndex)

    ' Real, confirmed intermittent finding: even with a generous polling ceiling (see below), a
    ' real Command Completion Event for THIS specific command sometimes never arrives at all, at
    ' essentially random points across a real multi-command sequence (confirmed via a raw Event
    ' Ring dump on failure: prior commands' own events were all present, correctly typed, and
    ' Success -- the ring and cycle-bit bookkeeping were genuinely fine, the doorbell's own effect
    ' just didn't happen this particular time). Root cause not conclusively pinned to one exact
    ' mechanism; worked around with a real, bounded RE-RING of the SAME already-enqueued TRB's
    ' doorbell (not a duplicate TRB submission) if a full polling pass comes up empty -- exactly
    ' the defensive retry shape a real xHCI driver uses for command timeouts. Confirmed empirically
    ' to restore full determinism across many consecutive real runs.
    LET eventBuffer AS MMIOPTR = XhciScratchEventBufferAddress()
    LET pollCeiling AS U64 = 2000000
    LET doorbellAttempt AS U32 = 0
    LET gotEvent AS BOOL = 0
    WHILE doorbellAttempt < 2
        XhciRingDoorbell(0, 0)
        LET pollAttempts AS U64 = 0
        WHILE pollAttempts < pollCeiling
            LET polled AS BOOL = XhciPollEvent(eventBuffer)
            IF polled = 1 THEN
                LET eventDword3 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(eventBuffer, 12))
                LET eventType AS U32 = (eventDword3 SHR 10) AND 63
                IF eventType = 33 THEN
                    gotEvent = 1
                    pollAttempts = pollCeiling
                ELSE
                    CPU.Pause
                    pollAttempts = pollAttempts + 1
                END IF
            ELSE
                CPU.Pause
                pollAttempts = pollAttempts + 1
            END IF
        WEND
        IF gotEvent = 1 THEN
            doorbellAttempt = 5
        ELSE
            doorbellAttempt = doorbellAttempt + 1
        END IF
    WEND
    IF gotEvent = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    LET eventDword2 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(eventBuffer, 8))
    LET completionCode AS U32 = (eventDword2 SHR 24) AND 255
    LET eventDword3b AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(eventBuffer, 12))
    LET slotId AS U32 = (eventDword3b SHR 24) AND 255
    MEMORY.Write32(outCompletionCode, completionCode)
    MEMORY.Write32(outSlotId, slotId)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Real Enable Slot Command (RFC-0045 Section 6.1's own device-enumeration prerequisite). Returns
' the real Slot ID (1-based) on success, 0 on failure -- CompletionCode 1 = Success.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.EnableSlot() AS U32
    LET completionCode AS U32 = 0
    LET completionCodeAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(completionCode)
    LET slotId AS U32 = 0
    LET slotIdAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(slotId)
    LET controlBits AS U32 = 9 SHL 10
    LET ok AS BOOL = XhciSubmitCommand(0, 0, 0, controlBits, completionCodeAddr, slotIdAddr)
    IF ok = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    IF completionCode <> 1 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciSlotIdAddress(), slotId)
    RETURN slotId
END FUNCTION

' Real Address Device Command: builds a real Input Context (Input Control Context + Slot Context +
' EP0 Endpoint Context, Context Size confirmed 32 bytes via HCCPARAMS1.CSZ -- see MapMmio), a real
' Device Context registered in the DCBAA at this slot's own index, and a real Transfer Ring for
' EP0 -- then issues the command and confirms real success.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.AddressDevice(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable, slotId AS U32, portIndex AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET inputCtxPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET inputCtxPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(inputCtxPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, inputCtxPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET inputCtxMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(inputCtxPhys))
    ' Zero the whole page first -- AllocatePages makes no zero-fill guarantee, and several
    ' Input/Slot/Endpoint Context dwords are RsvdZ (reserved, must-be-zero) fields this driver
    ' never explicitly writes; leftover allocator garbage there is a real spec violation.
    LET zeroCtxIndex AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroCtxIndex < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, zeroCtxIndex * 16), 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, zeroCtxIndex * 16 + 8), 0)
        zeroCtxIndex = zeroCtxIndex + 1
    WEND
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciInputCtxPhysAddress(), inputCtxPhys)
    LET inputCtxMmioAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(inputCtxMmio)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciInputCtxVirtAddress(), inputCtxMmioAsU64)

    LET deviceCtxPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET deviceCtxPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(deviceCtxPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, deviceCtxPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET deviceCtxMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(deviceCtxPhys))
    LET zeroDevCtxIndex AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroDevCtxIndex < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(deviceCtxMmio, zeroDevCtxIndex * 16), 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(deviceCtxMmio, zeroDevCtxIndex * 16 + 8), 0)
        zeroDevCtxIndex = zeroDevCtxIndex + 1
    WEND
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciDeviceCtxPhysAddress(), deviceCtxPhys)
    LET deviceCtxMmioAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(deviceCtxMmio)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciDeviceCtxVirtAddress(), deviceCtxMmioAsU64)

    LET dcbaaPhys AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciDcbaaPhysAddress())
    LET dcbaaMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(dcbaaPhys))
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(dcbaaMmio, slotId * 8), deviceCtxPhys)

    LET ep0RingPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET ep0RingPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(ep0RingPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, ep0RingPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET ep0RingMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(ep0RingPhys))
    LET zeroIndex AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroIndex < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(ep0RingMmio, zeroIndex * 16), 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(ep0RingMmio, zeroIndex * 16 + 8), 0)
        zeroIndex = zeroIndex + 1
    WEND
    LET linkOffset AS U32 = 255 * 16
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(ep0RingMmio, linkOffset), ep0RingPhys)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(ep0RingMmio, linkOffset + 8), 0)
    LET linkControl AS U32 = 1
    linkControl = linkControl OR (6 SHL 10)
    linkControl = linkControl OR 2
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(ep0RingMmio, linkOffset + 12), linkControl)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciEp0RingPhysAddress(), ep0RingPhys)
    LET ep0RingMmioAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(ep0RingMmio)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciEp0RingVirtAddress(), ep0RingMmioAsU64)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciEp0CycleStateAddress(), 1)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciEp0EnqueueIndexAddress(), 0)

    ' Input Control Context (offset 0, 32 bytes): Add Context flags A0 (Slot) and A1 (EP0).
    MEMORY.Write32(inputCtxMmio, 0)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 4), 3)

    ' Slot Context (offset 32): Route String=0 (root-connected), Speed from the real port's own
    ' PORTSC (bits 13:10), Context Entries=1 (only EP0 valid so far), Root Hub Port Number.
    LET portRaw AS U32 = UsbXhci.PortRaw(portIndex)
    LET portSpeed AS U32 = (portRaw SHR 10) AND 15
    LET slotDword0 AS U32 = 1 SHL 27
    slotDword0 = slotDword0 OR (portSpeed SHL 20)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 32), slotDword0)
    LET slotDword1 AS U32 = portIndex SHL 16
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 36), slotDword1)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 40), 0)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 44), 0)

    ' EP0 Endpoint Context (offset 64): EP Type=4 (Control), CErr=3, a conservative MaxPacketSize
    ' by real detected speed (Low-Speed=8, everything else starts at 64 -- a real, standard
    ' enumeration convention: the true value is learned from the device descriptor afterward).
    LET ep0MaxPacket AS U32 = 64
    IF portSpeed = 2 THEN
        ep0MaxPacket = 8
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciEp0MaxPacketAddress(), ep0MaxPacket)

    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 64), 0)
    LET ep0Dword1 AS U32 = 3 SHL 1
    ep0Dword1 = ep0Dword1 OR (4 SHL 3)
    ep0Dword1 = ep0Dword1 OR (ep0MaxPacket SHL 16)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 68), ep0Dword1)
    LET trDequeue AS U64 = ep0RingPhys OR 1
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 72), trDequeue)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 80), 8)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 84), 0)

    LET completionCode AS U32 = 0
    LET completionCodeAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(completionCode)
    LET outSlotId AS U32 = 0
    LET outSlotIdAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(outSlotId)
    LET inputCtxPhysLow AS U32 = inputCtxPhys AND 4294967295
    LET inputCtxPhysHigh AS U32 = inputCtxPhys SHR 32
    LET controlBits AS U32 = 11 SHL 10
    controlBits = controlBits OR (slotId SHL 24)
    LET ok AS BOOL = XhciSubmitCommand(inputCtxPhysLow, inputCtxPhysHigh, 0, controlBits, completionCodeAddr, outSlotIdAddr)
    IF ok = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    RETURN completionCode = 1
END FUNCTION

' Enqueues one TRB (dword0/1/2 verbatim, controlBits pre-shifted TRB Type/flags minus Cycle) onto
' the EP0 Transfer Ring, handling the same real ring-wrap-and-toggle-cycle idiom as the Command
' Ring (XhciSubmitCommand) and Interrupt Transfer Ring (below) -- three near-identical rings, three
' near-identical wrap handlers, kept separate because each ring's own cycle/enqueue state lives in
' its own dedicated state fields (mirrors XhciSubmitCommand's own established shape).
FUNCTION XhciEp0EnqueueTrb(dword0 AS U32, dword1 AS U32, dword2 AS U32, controlBits AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET ringVirt AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciEp0RingVirtAddress())
    LET enqueueIndex AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciEp0EnqueueIndexAddress())
    LET cycleState AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciEp0CycleStateAddress())
    LET ringMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(ringVirt))
    LET trbOffset AS U32 = enqueueIndex * 16
    LET trb AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(ringMmio, trbOffset)

    MEMORY.Write32(trb, dword0)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 4), dword1)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 8), dword2)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 12), controlBits OR cycleState)

    LET newIndex AS U32 = enqueueIndex + 1
    IF newIndex >= 255 THEN
        LET linkTrb AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(ringMmio, 255 * 16)
        LET linkControl AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(linkTrb, 12))
        LET linkControlBase AS U32 = linkControl AND 4294967294
        LET newCycle AS U32 = 1 - cycleState
        MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(linkTrb, 12), linkControlBase OR newCycle)
        MEMORY.Write32(XhciEp0CycleStateAddress(), newCycle)
        newIndex = 0
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciEp0EnqueueIndexAddress(), newIndex)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Real EP0 control transfer (Setup + optional Data + Status Stage TRBs -- the real xHCI shape for
' every USB control transfer, Section 4.11.2.2). IN-only data direction, matching this driver's own
' scope (GET_DESCRIPTOR + the no-data SET_CONFIGURATION/SET_PROTOCOL class/standard requests --
' RFC-0045 Phase 3 never needs an OUT data stage). Data lands in the shared scratch DMA buffer.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.Ep0ControlTransfer(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable, slotId AS U32, bmRequestType AS U32, bRequest AS U32, wValue AS U32, wIndex AS U32, wLength AS U32, hasData AS BOOL, outActualLength AS PTR) AS BOOL
    IF XhciEnsureScratchDmaBuffer(systemTable) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET setupDword0 AS U32 = bmRequestType OR (bRequest SHL 8) OR (wValue SHL 16)
    LET setupDword1 AS U32 = wIndex OR (wLength SHL 16)
    LET setupDword2 AS U32 = 8
    LET setupControl AS U32 = 1 SHL 6
    setupControl = setupControl OR (2 SHL 10)
    IF hasData = 1 THEN
        setupControl = setupControl OR (3 SHL 16)
    END IF
    XhciEp0EnqueueTrb(setupDword0, setupDword1, setupDword2, setupControl)

    IF hasData = 1 THEN
        LET dmaBufferPhys AS U64 = XhciScratchDmaPhys()
        LET dmaBufferPhysLow AS U32 = dmaBufferPhys AND 4294967295
        LET dmaBufferPhysHigh AS U32 = dmaBufferPhys SHR 32
        LET dataDword2 AS U32 = wLength
        LET dataControl AS U32 = 3 SHL 10
        dataControl = dataControl OR (1 SHL 16)
        XhciEp0EnqueueTrb(dmaBufferPhysLow, dmaBufferPhysHigh, dataDword2, dataControl)
    END IF

    LET statusControl AS U32 = 1 SHL 5
    statusControl = statusControl OR (4 SHL 10)
    IF hasData = 0 THEN
        statusControl = statusControl OR (1 SHL 16)
    END IF
    XhciEp0EnqueueTrb(0, 0, 0, statusControl)

    ' Same real, confirmed intermittent finding and same real fix as XhciSubmitCommand's own
    ' doorbell-retry loop (see its header comment) -- a bounded re-ring of the SAME already-
    ' enqueued TRB sequence's doorbell if a full polling pass comes up empty.
    LET eventBuffer AS MMIOPTR = XhciScratchEventBufferAddress()
    LET pollCeiling AS U64 = 2000000
    LET completionCode AS U32 = 0
    LET actualLength AS U32 = 0
    LET doorbellAttempt AS U32 = 0
    LET gotEvent AS BOOL = 0
    WHILE doorbellAttempt < 2
        XhciRingDoorbell(slotId, 1)
        LET pollAttempts AS U64 = 0
        WHILE pollAttempts < pollCeiling
            LET polled AS BOOL = XhciPollEvent(eventBuffer)
            IF polled = 1 THEN
                LET eventDword3 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(eventBuffer, 12))
                LET eventType AS U32 = (eventDword3 SHR 10) AND 63
                IF eventType = 32 THEN
                    LET eventDword2 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(eventBuffer, 8))
                    completionCode = (eventDword2 SHR 24) AND 255
                    actualLength = eventDword2 AND 16777215
                    gotEvent = 1
                    pollAttempts = pollCeiling
                ELSE
                    CPU.Pause
                    pollAttempts = pollAttempts + 1
                END IF
            ELSE
                CPU.Pause
                pollAttempts = pollAttempts + 1
            END IF
        WEND
        IF gotEvent = 1 THEN
            doorbellAttempt = 5
        ELSE
            doorbellAttempt = doorbellAttempt + 1
        END IF
    WEND
    IF gotEvent = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    ' The one Transfer Event this driver waits for is always the STATUS Stage TRB's own completion
    ' (IOC is deliberately only set there, not on the Data Stage TRB -- see the header comment on
    ' this driver's own real-bug findings) -- its "TRB Transfer Length" field is therefore always 0
    ' by construction and NOT the real data byte count. This driver's own GetDescriptor callers
    ' never over-request (8-byte device-descriptor probe, 9-byte config-header probe, then the
    ' device's own reported wTotalLength) so a real Success on the whole 3-stage transfer honestly
    ' implies the full wLength was really transferred; a real Short Packet on Data Stage would still
    ' surface as a Status-stage Success here (ISP/IOC weren't requested on Data Stage), a real,
    ' documented scope limitation rather than a silent miscount.
    LET reportedLength AS U32 = 0
    IF hasData = 1 THEN
        reportedLength = wLength
    END IF
    MEMORY.Write32(outActualLength, reportedLength)
    RETURN completionCode = 1
END FUNCTION

' GET_DESCRIPTOR (a real standard USB control request, bmRequestType=0x80 Device-to-Host/Standard/
' Device). Result bytes land in the shared scratch DMA buffer; returns actual bytes transferred.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.GetDescriptor(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable, slotId AS U32, descType AS U32, descIndex AS U32, wLength AS U32) AS U32
    LET wValue AS U32 = descIndex OR (descType SHL 8)
    LET actualLength AS U32 = 0
    LET actualLengthAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(actualLength)
    LET ok AS BOOL = UsbXhci.Ep0ControlTransfer(systemTable, slotId, 128, 6, wValue, 0, wLength, 1, actualLengthAddr)
    IF ok = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    RETURN actualLength
END FUNCTION

' SET_CONFIGURATION (standard request, no data stage) / SET_PROTOCOL (HID class request, no data
' stage, Boot Protocol=0) -- both share this same no-data control-transfer shape.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.Ep0NoDataRequest(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable, slotId AS U32, bmRequestType AS U32, bRequest AS U32, wValue AS U32, wIndex AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET actualLength AS U32 = 0
    LET actualLengthAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(actualLength)
    RETURN UsbXhci.Ep0ControlTransfer(systemTable, slotId, bmRequestType, bRequest, wValue, wIndex, 0, 0, actualLengthAddr)
END FUNCTION

' Real xHCI Interval-field encoding for a Low/Full-Speed interrupt endpoint (Section 6.2.3.6): the
' device's own bInterval is expressed in frames (1-255); xHCI wants floor(log2(bInterval)) + 3,
' clamped to the valid 3..10 range for LS/FS. Computed via a real bit-shift loop, not a table --
' this driver has no floating point / log() available on this freestanding backend.
FUNCTION XhciComputeLsFsInterval(bInterval AS U32) AS U32
    LET frames AS U32 = bInterval
    IF frames < 1 THEN
        frames = 1
    END IF
    LET exponent AS U32 = 0
    LET probe AS U32 = 1
    WHILE probe * 2 <= frames
        probe = probe * 2
        exponent = exponent + 1
    WEND
    LET result AS U32 = exponent + 3
    IF result > 10 THEN
        result = 10
    END IF
    RETURN result
END FUNCTION

' Real Configure Endpoint Command (TRB Type 12): registers this device's own HID interrupt IN
' endpoint (discovered by parsing its configuration descriptor) with the controller -- Interval
' converted via the real LS/FS formula above, Endpoint Type=7 (Interrupt IN) per Table 6-9.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.ConfigureHidEndpoint(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable, slotId AS U32, endpointAddress AS U32, maxPacketSize AS U32, bInterval AS U32) AS BOOL
    LET inputCtxVirt AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciInputCtxVirtAddress())
    LET inputCtxMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(inputCtxVirt))

    LET epNum AS U32 = endpointAddress AND 15
    LET dci AS U32 = epNum * 2 + 1
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntContextIndexAddress(), dci)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntEndpointAddrAddress(), endpointAddress)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntMaxPacketAddress(), maxPacketSize)
    LET intervalField AS U32 = XhciComputeLsFsInterval(bInterval)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntIntervalAddress(), intervalField)

    ' Re-zero the Input Context (a stale Address Device configuration may still be sitting in it)
    ' before laying down this command's own Add Context flags / Slot / Endpoint fields.
    LET zeroIndex AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroIndex < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, zeroIndex * 16), 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, zeroIndex * 16 + 8), 0)
        zeroIndex = zeroIndex + 1
    WEND

    LET addFlags AS U32 = 1
    addFlags = addFlags OR (1 SHL dci)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 4), addFlags)

    LET deviceCtxVirt AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciDeviceCtxVirtAddress())
    LET deviceCtxMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(deviceCtxVirt))
    LET existingSlotDword0 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(deviceCtxMmio)
    LET slotDword0Base AS U32 = existingSlotDword0 AND 134217727
    LET slotDword0New AS U32 = slotDword0Base OR (dci SHL 27)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 32), slotDword0New)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 36), MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(deviceCtxMmio, 4)))
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 40), MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(deviceCtxMmio, 8)))
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, 44), 0)

    LET intRingPhys AS U64 = 0
    LET intRingPhysAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(intRingPhys)
    IF XhciAllocPage(systemTable, intRingPhysAddr) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET intRingMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(intRingPhys))
    LET zeroRingIndex AS U32 = 0
    WHILE zeroRingIndex < 256
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(intRingMmio, zeroRingIndex * 16), 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(intRingMmio, zeroRingIndex * 16 + 8), 0)
        zeroRingIndex = zeroRingIndex + 1
    WEND
    LET linkOffset AS U32 = 255 * 16
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(intRingMmio, linkOffset), intRingPhys)
    LET linkControl AS U32 = 1
    linkControl = linkControl OR (6 SHL 10)
    linkControl = linkControl OR 2
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(intRingMmio, linkOffset + 12), linkControl)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciIntRingPhysAddress(), intRingPhys)
    LET intRingMmioAsU64 AS U64 = ADDRESS.Value(intRingMmio)
    MEMORY.Write64(XhciIntRingVirtAddress(), intRingMmioAsU64)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntCycleStateAddress(), 1)
    MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntEnqueueIndexAddress(), 0)

    LET epCtxOffset AS U32 = (1 + dci) * 32
    ' Real, confirmed bit-position bug found and fixed: dword0's real layout (cross-checked
    ' directly against QEMU's own xhci_init_epctx parsing, hw/usb/hcd-xhci.c) is Mult at bits 0-1,
    ' Max Primary Streams at bits 10-14, LSA at bit 15, Interval at bits 16-23 -- NOT Interval at
    ' bits 8-15 as this driver originally (wrongly) placed it. That earlier placement's own nonzero
    ' Interval value bled into bit 10, which QEMU reads as part of Max Primary Streams -- making a
    ' plain, non-streaming endpoint look stream-capable to the controller, which then genuinely
    ' aborted the whole QEMU process on the very first doorbell ring (hw/usb/hcd-xhci.c's own
    ' `assert(streamid != 0)` in xhci_find_stream, since this driver never uses stream IDs and
    ' always rings with Stream ID 0). Found by reading QEMU's own source after the crash, not by
    ' spec inspection alone -- Max Primary Streams/LSA are left at 0 here (non-streaming), matching
    ' this driver's own real scope (one boot-protocol keyboard, no stream support).
    LET epDword0 AS U32 = intervalField SHL 16
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, epCtxOffset), epDword0)
    LET epDword1 AS U32 = 3 SHL 1
    epDword1 = epDword1 OR (7 SHL 3)
    epDword1 = epDword1 OR (maxPacketSize SHL 16)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, epCtxOffset + 4), epDword1)
    LET trDequeue AS U64 = intRingPhys OR 1
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, epCtxOffset + 8), trDequeue)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, epCtxOffset + 16), maxPacketSize)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(inputCtxMmio, epCtxOffset + 20), 0)

    LET inputCtxPhys AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciInputCtxPhysAddress())
    LET inputCtxPhysLow AS U32 = inputCtxPhys AND 4294967295
    LET inputCtxPhysHigh AS U32 = inputCtxPhys SHR 32
    LET controlBits AS U32 = 12 SHL 10
    controlBits = controlBits OR (slotId SHL 24)
    LET completionCode AS U32 = 0
    LET completionCodeAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(completionCode)
    LET outSlotId AS U32 = 0
    LET outSlotIdAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(outSlotId)
    LET ok AS BOOL = XhciSubmitCommand(inputCtxPhysLow, inputCtxPhysHigh, 0, controlBits, completionCodeAddr, outSlotIdAddr)
    IF ok = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    RETURN completionCode = 1
END FUNCTION

' Reads the parsed configuration descriptor (already sitting in the shared scratch DMA buffer, laid
' out as a flat run of Configuration + Interface + [HID] + Endpoint descriptors -- the real on-the-
' wire USB descriptor chain shape) and returns TRUE with the HID interrupt IN endpoint's own
' address/max-packet-size/interval if one was found (a real boot-protocol keyboard always has
' exactly one). A real, honest negative result (FALSE) if no such endpoint exists in the chain.
FUNCTION UsbXhci.FindHidInterruptEndpoint(totalLength AS U32, outEndpointAddress AS PTR, outMaxPacketSize AS PTR, outInterval AS PTR) AS BOOL
    LET dmaBufferMmio AS MMIOPTR = XhciScratchDmaMmio()
    LET cursor AS U32 = 0
    LET sawHidInterface AS BOOL = 0
    WHILE cursor + 2 <= totalLength
        LET descPtr AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(dmaBufferMmio, cursor)
        LET bLength AS U32 = MmioReadField32(descPtr, 0, 0, 8)
        LET bDescriptorType AS U32 = MmioReadField32(descPtr, 0, 8, 8)
        IF bLength < 2 THEN
            RETURN 0
        END IF
        IF bDescriptorType = 4 THEN
            ' Real, confirmed off-by-one bug found and fixed: bInterfaceClass lives at BYTE OFFSET
            ' 5 in a standard USB Interface Descriptor (0=bLength, 1=bDescriptorType,
            ' 2=bInterfaceNumber, 3=bAlternateSetting, 4=bNumEndpoints, 5=bInterfaceClass, ...) --
            ' offset 4 is bNumEndpoints, which for a boot-protocol keyboard misreads as "1" and
            ' silently never matches Class 3 (HID), so the HID interrupt endpoint below was never
            ' recognized (EP/MP always 0). Caught by a real byte-level dump of a real device's own
            ' configuration descriptor under QEMU, not by inspection alone.
            LET bInterfaceClass AS U32 = MmioReadField32(descPtr, 5, 0, 8)
            IF bInterfaceClass = 3 THEN
                sawHidInterface = 1
            ELSE
                sawHidInterface = 0
            END IF
        END IF
        IF bDescriptorType = 5 THEN
            IF sawHidInterface = 1 THEN
                LET bEndpointAddress AS U32 = MmioReadField32(descPtr, 2, 0, 8)
                LET bmAttributes AS U32 = MmioReadField32(descPtr, 3, 0, 8)
                LET isIn AS U32 = (bEndpointAddress SHR 7) AND 1
                LET transferType AS U32 = bmAttributes AND 3
                IF isIn = 1 THEN
                    IF transferType = 3 THEN
                        LET wMaxPacketSize AS U32 = MmioReadField32(descPtr, 4, 0, 16)
                        LET bInterval AS U32 = MmioReadField32(descPtr, 6, 0, 8)
                        MEMORY.Write32(outEndpointAddress, bEndpointAddress)
                        MEMORY.Write32(outMaxPacketSize, wMaxPacketSize)
                        MEMORY.Write32(outInterval, bInterval)
                        RETURN 1
                    END IF
                END IF
            END IF
        END IF
        cursor = cursor + bLength
    WEND
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

' Full real Phase 3 device bring-up: Enable Slot -> Address Device -> GET_DESCRIPTOR(Device, 8
' bytes, just to confirm the device answers) -> GET_DESCRIPTOR(Configuration, 9 bytes, to learn
' wTotalLength) -> GET_DESCRIPTOR(Configuration, wTotalLength, the real full descriptor chain) ->
' parse for the HID interrupt IN endpoint -> Configure Endpoint -> SET_CONFIGURATION ->
' SET_PROTOCOL(Boot Protocol). Returns the real Slot ID on success, 0 on any real failure.
FUNCTION UsbHidKeyboard.Init(systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable, portIndex AS U32) AS U32
    LET slotId AS U32 = UsbXhci.EnableSlot()
    IF slotId = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    IF UsbXhci.AddressDevice(systemTable, slotId, portIndex) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    LET devDescLen AS U32 = UsbXhci.GetDescriptor(systemTable, slotId, 1, 0, 8)
    IF devDescLen = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    LET cfgHeaderLen AS U32 = UsbXhci.GetDescriptor(systemTable, slotId, 2, 0, 9)
    IF cfgHeaderLen < 4 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET cfgHeaderMmio AS MMIOPTR = XhciScratchDmaMmio()
    LET wTotalLength AS U32 = MmioReadField32(cfgHeaderMmio, 2, 0, 16)
    LET bConfigurationValue AS U32 = MmioReadField32(cfgHeaderMmio, 5, 0, 8)
    IF wTotalLength > 256 THEN
        wTotalLength = 256
    END IF

    LET fullCfgLen AS U32 = UsbXhci.GetDescriptor(systemTable, slotId, 2, 0, wTotalLength)
    IF fullCfgLen = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    LET endpointAddress AS U32 = 0
    LET endpointAddressAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(endpointAddress)
    LET maxPacketSize AS U32 = 0
    LET maxPacketSizeAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(maxPacketSize)
    LET bInterval AS U32 = 0
    LET bIntervalAddr AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(bInterval)
    LET found AS BOOL = UsbXhci.FindHidInterruptEndpoint(fullCfgLen, endpointAddressAddr, maxPacketSizeAddr, bIntervalAddr)
    IF found = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    IF UsbXhci.ConfigureHidEndpoint(systemTable, slotId, endpointAddress, maxPacketSize, bInterval) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    IF UsbXhci.Ep0NoDataRequest(systemTable, slotId, 0, 9, bConfigurationValue, 0) = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    UsbXhci.Ep0NoDataRequest(systemTable, slotId, 33, 11, 0, 0)

    RETURN slotId
END FUNCTION

' Real, non-blocking "is a new HID report ready" check -- matches PS2Keyboard.PollScancode's own
' established sibling contract exactly (RFC-0045's own two input paths sharing one polling shape):
' a single Event Ring check, no internal busy-wait. The first call (or the first call after a prior
' report was consumed) submits one new Normal TRB on the Interrupt IN endpoint's own Transfer Ring
' and rings its doorbell; that request then stays outstanding (tracked in state, so repeat calls
' before a response arrives do NOT re-submit a duplicate TRB) until a real Transfer Event completes
' it. Callers are expected to poll this in their own loop, exactly like PS2Keyboard.PollScancode.
FUNCTION UsbHidKeyboard.PollReport(slotId AS U32, out8ByteReport AS MMIOPTR) AS BOOL
    LET pending AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciIntRequestPendingAddress())
    IF pending = 0 THEN
        LET ringVirt AS U64 = MEMORY.Read64(XhciIntRingVirtAddress())
        LET enqueueIndex AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciIntEnqueueIndexAddress())
        LET cycleState AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciIntCycleStateAddress())
        LET ringMmio AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(ringVirt))
        LET trbOffset AS U32 = enqueueIndex * 16
        LET trb AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(ringMmio, trbOffset)

        LET dmaBufferPhys AS U64 = XhciScratchDmaPhys()
        LET dmaBufferPhysLow AS U32 = dmaBufferPhys AND 4294967295
        LET dmaBufferPhysHigh AS U32 = dmaBufferPhys SHR 32
        MEMORY.Write32(trb, dmaBufferPhysLow)
        MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 4), dmaBufferPhysHigh)
        MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 8), 8)
        LET control AS U32 = 1 SHL 2
        control = control OR (1 SHL 5)
        control = control OR (1 SHL 10)
        MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(trb, 12), control OR cycleState)

        LET newIndex AS U32 = enqueueIndex + 1
        IF newIndex >= 255 THEN
            LET linkTrb AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(ringMmio, 255 * 16)
            LET linkControl AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(linkTrb, 12))
            LET linkControlBase AS U32 = linkControl AND 4294967294
            LET newCycle AS U32 = 1 - cycleState
            MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(linkTrb, 12), linkControlBase OR newCycle)
            MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntCycleStateAddress(), newCycle)
            newIndex = 0
        END IF
        MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntEnqueueIndexAddress(), newIndex)

        LET dci AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(XhciIntContextIndexAddress())
        XhciRingDoorbell(slotId, dci)
        MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntRequestPendingAddress(), 1)
    END IF

    LET eventBuffer AS MMIOPTR = XhciScratchEventBufferAddress()
    LET polled AS BOOL = XhciPollEvent(eventBuffer)
    IF polled = 0 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF
    LET eventDword3 AS U32 = MEMORY.Read32(ADDRESS.Offset(eventBuffer, 12))
    LET eventType AS U32 = (eventDword3 SHR 10) AND 63
    IF eventType <> 32 THEN
        RETURN 0
    END IF

    MEMORY.Write32(XhciIntRequestPendingAddress(), 0)
    LET dmaBufferMmio AS MMIOPTR = XhciScratchDmaMmio()
    MEMORY.Write64(out8ByteReport, MEMORY.Read64(dmaBufferMmio))
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

' Real USB HID Keyboard/Keypad Usage Page (0x07) translation -- boot-protocol report byte layout is
' fixed: byte0=modifiers, byte1=reserved, bytes2-7=up to 6 simultaneous keycodes. US QWERTY
' unshifted only (matches RFC-0045's own Non-Goals; PS2Keyboard.ScancodeToChar is this driver's own
' established sibling for the exact same scope decision). Fail-closed (0) for anything undefined.
FUNCTION UsbHidKeyboard.KeycodeToChar(keycode AS U32) AS U32
    IF keycode >= 4 THEN
        IF keycode <= 29 THEN
            RETURN keycode - 4 + 97
        END IF
    END IF
    IF keycode >= 30 THEN
        IF keycode <= 38 THEN
            RETURN keycode - 30 + 49
        END IF
    END IF
    IF keycode = 39 THEN
        RETURN 48
    END IF
    IF keycode = 40 THEN
        RETURN 13
    END IF
    IF keycode = 42 THEN
        RETURN 8
    END IF
    IF keycode = 43 THEN
        RETURN 9
    END IF
    IF keycode = 44 THEN
        RETURN 32
    END IF
    IF keycode = 45 THEN
        RETURN 45
    END IF
    IF keycode = 46 THEN
        RETURN 61
    END IF
    IF keycode = 51 THEN
        RETURN 59
    END IF
    IF keycode = 52 THEN
        RETURN 39
    END IF
    IF keycode = 54 THEN
        RETURN 44
    END IF
    IF keycode = 55 THEN
        RETURN 46
    END IF
    IF keycode = 56 THEN
        RETURN 47
    END IF
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION



' APS GDT-replacement proof. Extends aps-breakpoint-recovery.abas: instead of keeping the
' firmware's own GDT (that fixture's deliberate scope limit), this one builds a genuinely new,
' independent GDT and TSS within the APS-owned identity-mapped region, activates them via
' CPU.LoadGDT + CPU.ReloadCodeSegment (a far return -- the only way to change CS in 64-bit mode;
' see x86_64_encoder.hpp's retfq()), then proves it actually took effect two ways: a live CS
' readback matches the new table's own code-segment selector (8, not whatever the firmware had),
' and a deliberate CPU.Breakpoint recovers correctly using gates built against that new selector --
' meaning the new GDT's code descriptor is genuinely what the CPU is running under, not just
' loaded and ignored. Closes the "Segment-selector reload" gate aps-owned-gdt.md and
' aps-exception-entry-stub.md both left open.

FUNCTION SerialByte(value AS U8) AS U64
    LET port AS IOPORT = PORT.Address(1016)
    LET statusPort AS IOPORT = PORT.Offset(port, 5)
    LET attempts AS U32 = 0
    WHILE (PORT.ReadByte(statusPort) AND 32) = 0
        CPU.Pause
        attempts = attempts + 1
        IF attempts >= 10000 THEN
            RETURN 1
        END IF
    WEND
    PORT.WriteByte(port, value)
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION SerialInit() AS U64
    LET base AS IOPORT = PORT.Address(1016)
    PORT.WriteByte(PORT.Offset(base, 1), 0)
    PORT.WriteByte(PORT.Offset(base, 3), 128)
    PORT.WriteByte(base, 1)
    PORT.WriteByte(PORT.Offset(base, 1), 0)
    PORT.WriteByte(PORT.Offset(base, 3), 3)
    PORT.WriteByte(PORT.Offset(base, 2), 199)
    PORT.WriteByte(PORT.Offset(base, 4), 11)
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

' Mirrors stdlib/descriptor_table_policy.abas (inlined -- this build takes a single source file).
FUNCTION DescriptorWrite64(table AS MMIOPTR, offset AS U32, value AS U64) AS U64
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(table, offset), value)
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION BuildTSS(tss AS MMIOPTR, ringZeroStack AS U64, doubleFaultStack AS U64) AS BOOL
    LET offset AS U32 = 0
    WHILE offset < 104
        MEMORY.Write8(ADDRESS.Offset(tss, offset), 0)
        offset = offset + 1
    WEND
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(tss, 4), ringZeroStack)
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(tss, 36), doubleFaultStack)
    MEMORY.Write16(ADDRESS.Offset(tss, 102), 104)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION BuildTSSDescriptor(table AS MMIOPTR, offset AS U32, tssBase AS U64) AS BOOL
    LET low AS U64 = 103
    low = low OR ((tssBase AND 65535) SHL 16)
    low = low OR (((tssBase SHR 16) AND 255) SHL 32)
    low = low OR (137 SHL 40)
    low = low OR (((tssBase SHR 24) AND 255) SHL 56)
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(table, offset), low)
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(table, offset + 8), (tssBase SHR 32) AND 4294967295)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION BuildMinimalGDT(table AS MMIOPTR, pseudoDescriptor AS MMIOPTR, tssBase AS U64) AS BOOL
    ' Null, 64-bit code, long-mode data, and one available 64-bit TSS.
    DescriptorWrite64(table, 0, 0)
    DescriptorWrite64(table, 8, 49427445715107839)
    DescriptorWrite64(table, 16, 58425848876826623)
    BuildTSSDescriptor(table, 24, tssBase)
    MEMORY.Write16(ADDRESS.Offset(pseudoDescriptor, 0), 39)
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(pseudoDescriptor, 2), ADDRESS.Value(table))
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION IDTWriteInterruptGate(table AS MMIOPTR, index AS U32, handler AS U64, codeSelector AS U16, ist AS U8) AS BOOL
    LET gate AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(table, index * 16)
    MEMORY.Write16(gate, handler AND 65535)
    MEMORY.Write16(ADDRESS.Offset(gate, 2), codeSelector)
    MEMORY.Write8(ADDRESS.Offset(gate, 4), ist AND 7)
    MEMORY.Write8(ADDRESS.Offset(gate, 5), 142)
    MEMORY.Write16(ADDRESS.Offset(gate, 6), (handler SHR 16) AND 65535)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(gate, 8), (handler SHR 32) AND 4294967295)
    MEMORY.Write32(ADDRESS.Offset(gate, 12), 0)
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION BuildMinimalIDT(table AS MMIOPTR, pseudoDescriptor AS MMIOPTR, codeSelector AS U16) AS BOOL
    LET index AS U32 = 0
    WHILE index < 256
        LET gate AS MMIOPTR = ADDRESS.Offset(table, index * 16)
        MEMORY.Write64(gate, 0)
        MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(gate, 8), 0)
        index = index + 1
    WEND
    LET entry AS U64 = CPU.ExceptionVectorTableBase()
    LET vector AS U32 = 0
    WHILE vector < 32
        LET ist AS U8 = 0
        IF vector = 8 THEN ist = 1
        IDTWriteInterruptGate(table, vector, entry, codeSelector, ist)
        entry = entry + 16
        vector = vector + 1
    WEND
    MEMORY.Write16(ADDRESS.Offset(pseudoDescriptor, 0), 4095)
    MEMORY.Write64(ADDRESS.Offset(pseudoDescriptor, 2), ADDRESS.Value(table))
    RETURN 1
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ActivateDescriptorTables(gdtPseudo AS U64, idtPseudo AS U64, tssSelector AS U64, codeSelector AS U64) AS U64
    CPU.LoadGDT(gdtPseudo)
    CPU.ReloadCodeSegment(codeSelector)
    CPU.LoadTaskRegister(tssSelector)
    CPU.LoadIDT(idtPseudo)
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION AcquireMapAndExit(imageHandle AS UEFI.Handle, systemTable AS UEFI.SystemTable) AS U64
    LET mapSize AS U64 = 0
    LET mapSizeAddress AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(mapSize)
    LET probe AS U64 = systemTable.BootServices.GetMemoryMap(mapSizeAddress, 0, 0, 0, 0)
    IF mapSize = 0 THEN
        RETURN 1
    END IF
    LET allocationSize AS U64 = mapSize + 65536
    LET buffer AS U64 = 0
    LET bufferAddress AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(buffer)
    LET allocate AS U64 = systemTable.BootServices.AllocatePool(2, allocationSize, bufferAddress)
    IF allocate <> 0 THEN
        RETURN 1
    END IF
    mapSize = allocationSize
    LET mapKey AS U64 = 0
    LET mapKeyAddress AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(mapKey)
    LET descriptorSize AS U64 = 0
    LET descriptorSizeAddress AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(descriptorSize)
    LET descriptorVersion AS U32 = 0
    LET descriptorVersionAddress AS PTR = ADDRESS.Local(descriptorVersion)
    LET status AS U64 = systemTable.BootServices.GetMemoryMap(mapSizeAddress, buffer, mapKeyAddress, descriptorSizeAddress, descriptorVersionAddress)
    IF status <> 0 THEN
        systemTable.BootServices.FreePool(buffer)
        RETURN 1
    END IF
    IF descriptorSize < 48 THEN
        systemTable.BootServices.FreePool(buffer)
        RETURN 1
    END IF
    RETURN systemTable.BootServices.ExitBootServices(imageHandle, mapKey)
END FUNCTION

' Real 8x8 bitmap font (ASCII 32-126, 95 glyphs), rendered offline from a real monospace
' TrueType font (FreeMonoBold) and embedded here as 95 packed U64 constants (one write per
' glyph, byte[row]=8-bit row pattern, bit7=leftmost pixel) -- RFC-0045 Phase 5's own real
' need: a genuinely on-screen READY. terminal, since the substrate's own post-ExitBootServices
' output (serial only, see aps-gdt-reload.abas/ps2-keyboard-driver.abas) isn't observable on
' real hardware without a serial capture setup most laptops don't expose.
FUNCTION FontTableAddress() AS MMIOPTR
    RETURN ADDRESS.MMIO(ADDRESS.Virtual(50331648))   ' 0x3000000, clear of every other fixed scratch region this fixture uses
END FUNCTION

